      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "The amount of things they glossed over and didn’t think about before pushing this update is actually awful. Yes, Unity‑6 runs a bit better, but that didn’t require a whole redesign of the menu and profile system. Just because you can update something because you personally think it’s better doesn’t mean the player base or community feels the same way. It honestly feels like the people who decided this was a “good idea” knew very well their wallets would like it more than the players they were pushing it onto.\n\nThe redesign does nothing for the social tabs other than complicate the way things look, feel, and function. Even the redesign of the overhead nameplate is not well thought through; people’s group statuses and pronouns are all squished together, making them harder to see and read. For a game named after talking and finding friends on a VR platform, the decision to add features that shouldn’t—and are not—the main focus of the gameplay leaves a bad aftertaste and an even worse outlook on the direction the developers are actively taking the game.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
